The '''1999 Football League Cup final''' was played between [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]] and [[Leicester City F.C.|Leicester City]], at [[Wembley Stadium (1923)|Wembley]] on Sunday, 21 March 1999.

Tottenham won the game, and their third League Cup, with an injury-time diving header from [[Allan Nielsen]] after a cross from the right from [[Steffen Iversen]] had been blocked by goalkeeper [[Kasey Keller]].<ref>{{cite web|url = http://hotspurhq.com/2014/03/21/tottenham-day-league-cup-final-success-leicester-city/|title=Leicester 0 Spurs 1|work=hotspurhq.com|access-date=7 October 2014}}</ref> [[Justin Edinburgh]] became the last player to be sent off at the [[Wembley Stadium (1923)|old Wembley]], after angrily waving his arm towards [[Robbie Savage]] following a particularly tough Savage challenge.  In the last few minutes of the game, [[Ramon Vega]] made a last-ditch sliding tackle to deny [[Emile Heskey]] a goal for Leicester, after [[Ian Walker (footballer)|Ian Walker]] rushed off his line, and Allan Nielsen scored a diving header.<ref>{{cite web|url = https://www.spursodyssey.com/articles/wcfin1.html|title=Leicester 0 Spurs 1|work=Spursodyssey|access-date=7 October 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url = http://www.lcfc.com/news/article/190314-twih-1999-league-cup-final-1431026.aspx|title=1999 League Cup Final|work=lcfc.com|access-date=7 October 2014}}</ref>

